# Copy to functions/.env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is
# the shape of it, not a place for real values.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# A media server (LiveKit). The only shape that carries a whole class.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# In a direct call between browsers everybody sends their own video to
# everybody else: six people is five uploads each, sixty is fifty-nine
# from one laptop, which does not go slowly, it fails. A media server
# takes one stream from each person and forwards it, so sixty costs a
# participant what six does.
#
# It is also what makes the lesson genuinely in-app: LogicClass draws
# the video in its own widgets, so there is no embedded page for a
# server to refuse -- which is where two public Jitsi deployments left
# this feature. See docs/44-a-class-of-sixty.md.
#
# Set all three or none. Anyone holding the secret can mint entry to
# any lesson.
LIVEKIT_URL=
LIVEKIT_API_KEY=
LIVEKIT_API_SECRET=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The embedded path (Jitsi). Only for a school already on its own.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Nothing below is required, and none of it is read when LIVEKIT_* is
# set. Left unset entirely, the app joins its video classes without a
# token -- right on a deployment that asks for none, and that
# deployment's own sign-in on one that does.

# The tenant. `app_id` on a self-hosted Jitsi, the AppID on a JaaS tenant.
JITSI_APP_ID=

# Self-hosted: the matching `app_secret`, signed HS256.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
# Anyone holding this can mint entry to any lesson.
JITSI_APP_SECRET=

# JaaS instead of the above: the RSA private key, PEM, and its key id.
# Paste as it comes -- escaped newlines are put back by the reader.
# JITSI_KEY_ID is the key id from the console (vpaas-magic-cookie-.../a1b2c3),
# not the AppID; it goes in the JWT header and a token without it is
# rejected with nothing useful said about why. See docs/43.
JITSI_PRIVATE_KEY=
JITSI_KEY_ID=

# Where the classes are held -- 8x8.vc for a JaaS tenant. Must match the
# JITSI_DOMAIN Actions variable the web build uses, or every token is
# rejected by a server it was not minted for.
#
# The build also needs JITSI_TENANT (the AppID) as an Actions variable
# for a hosted tenant. It is not read here -- rooms are addressed by the
# client -- and leaving it out is the quiet failure: a conference at the
# wrong path with nobody in it.
JITSI_DOMAIN=
